Add /healthz, a readiness probe that answers 503 until the engine serves.

/health answers HTTP 200 in every lifecycle state, which includes "loading"
and "error". A process supervisor that reads only the status code, such as
llama-swap, therefore accepts a loading or dead engine as ready and sends it
traffic. /health keeps its behaviour, because the desktop app and the daemon
proxy read its body for load progress. This adds a second route for
supervisors.

